{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If he comes in by himself.</b> That he was not married — as the Targum renders: אִם בִּלְחוֹדוֹהִי. And the expression בְּגַפּוֹ — בִּכְנָפוֹ, 'in his corner,' that he came only as he is, alone, inside his clothing — בְּכְנַף בִּגְדוֹ." "<b>By himself he shall go out.</b> This teaches that if he was not married from the start, his master may not give him a Canaanite maidservant to beget slaves from her (Kiddushin 20)." "<b>If he is a husband of a wife.</b> An Israelite woman." "<b>And his wife shall go out with him.</b> But who brought her in that she should go out? Rather, Scripture teaches that one who acquires a Hebrew slave is obligated for the food of his wife and his children (ibid. 22)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:27.004643606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}